  "note": "Two encodings on one page. Lines 2-6 are ROLE-THEN-NAME in two column pairs ('Principal / Timothy Santry' on the left, 'Admin. Assistant / Tina Cooney' on the right). From line 7 the page becomes bare-name columns under department headings (Math, Language Arts, Science, Social Studies, Foreign Language, Unified Arts), with no role printed at all -- those entries carry role_raw '' and the department in grade_or_dept. The asterisk after a name is kept as printed in name AND recorded as role_raw '*' so the marker is machine-visible: page 139 line 16 prints the legend '*Department Head', so an asterisk here marks a department head. TWO JUDGEMENT CALLS, stated openly. (1) Line 6 'Kelly Scott' is printed alone at column 86. That is the right-hand column position that holds ROLE labels on lines 2-3 ('Admin. Assistant' at 90, 'Secretary' at 88) and NAMES from line 8 onward ('Warren Stevenson*' at 89, 'Brent Coxall' at 89); no role is printed with her either way; she is recorded as an entry with role_raw '' and grade_or_dept '', though she may belong with 'Nurse / Lisa Lavery' on line 5 (page 134 lists a Kelly Scott as the Middle School '(LPN)'). (2) Line 22 prints 'Brent Coxall' in the right-hand column with 'IT Dept.' to his right. Applying the column rule mechanically would give him the nearest heading above in that column, 'Social Studies', which is plainly wrong -- he carries his own role label. The row in fact follows the lines 2-3 layout (a label column at ~88 and a value column at ~122) with the two swapped: 'Brent Coxall' at 89, 'IT Dept.' at 129. He is recorded with role_raw 'IT Dept.' and grade_or_dept ''; page 134 lists him under 'Technology IT:'. LIKELY READING: line 20 'James MeSweeney' is probably 'James McSweeney'. Timothy Santry is listed on page 134 as 'LMHS Principal' -- the Middle and High Schools share him.",
